REQUEST / PRIORITIES
Implement Inventory Reports under Tools, using the existing card aesthetic and
an appropriate chart, referenced from Figma MAc7bCMKF4RDYbCYQetqt9 node 1:3.
POS remains excluded; automatic sync remains last priority. Receiving, physical
counts and variance entry are separate pending workflows, not invented data.
Continue the requested fresh-schema testing workflow: no compatibility/upgrades.

IMPLEMENTED
- Tools Reports opens Inventory Reports; Stock Movements is a separate subpage.
  Each page has its own Kotlin file and string resource file. Existing chevron,
  fixed title/filter controls, portrait behavior and bottom navigation reused.
- Reference inspected with Figma design context and screenshot. Reuses pale blue
  rounded cards, red warnings, serif labels and large thin condensed values.
  Existing Material icons substitute the reference icons as authorized. No new
  chart dependency, image asset, palette color or sample business records added.
- Current stock report: active product units, low/out-of-stock counts and stock
  estimated at current selling prices. This is explicitly not cost/revenue/profit.
  Negative balances remain in net unit totals; only positive on-hand quantities
  contribute to value/chart. A negative-stock explanation appears when relevant.
  BigInteger valuation prevents Long multiplication/sum overflow.
- Horizontal bars compare units on hand by vendor using a common scale and
  numeric labels; zero-stock vendors display zero without a fake bar. No pie
  chart because vendor names and quantities read more clearly as labeled bars.
- Existing stock/vendor/category filter bottom sheet drives current cards,
  chart and product rows together. Clear restores all active products. Empty
  installs and no-match filters show honest empty states. Product rows open
  existing details. Scrolling is isolated to the report body.
- Stock Movements: all recorded opening/imported activity, added/removed/net
  units and dated reason/type/product rows. Separate date and vendor sheets;
  all dates defaults, including archived products and vendors. Vendor filtering
  uses the product's current assignment, disclosed in the filter sheet.
  Date filtering applies to recorded activity, not historical stock balances.
- Room movement observation flows into ShopState. Both pages update after local
  changes/imports/reset and work offline without Google/network requests.
  Shared date filtering now accepts timestamps and retains existing receipt rules.
- No database columns, worksheet headers, schema versions, migrations or sync
  behavior changed. No POS, receiving/count entry or automatic sync added.
- Updated prototype status and device acceptance checklist.

